== ARCHIVE: rho_floor sensitivity sweep (Step D) ==

Archived 2026-10-01. paper/main.md cites four measured numbers from this run -
10.7-22.6% of grid points dropped, the 2.1e-11 Ha span of E_AB across the accepted
floor interval, the 4.2e-11 Ha figure at the next grid level, and at most 2.3e-6
electrons carried by the dropped points - and until now their only carrier was
nlcsplit/logs/step_d_floor.out, which is gitignored scratch. By this repository's own
rule a working log is not citable as evidence, so the claim was citing a file no reader
can open. The body below is that file's content, verbatim; its SHA-256 is
45096418b755cb1884918ce90d1758417e930b691df9498eb2cf5027606ac3f7.

Run: PYTHONPATH=. python3 nlcsplit/step_d_floor.py
     water dimer (S22 initial structure), 6-31g*, wb97x_v, grid levels 1 and 2,
     floors 1e-8 / 1e-10 / 1e-12 / 1e-14 / 1e-16, 905 s total,
     PySCF 2.12.1 on Python 3.10.12. The filename is the completion time of the run in
     UTC (the source log's mtime, 2026-09-28 23:02:22 +08:00). The last commit before that
     moment is 45bc3b1; the run tested the working tree, which may have carried
     uncommitted changes, so this archive names no commit as the one under test.

Read the numbers out of the 判读 block near the end: the accepted interval is floors
1e-10..1e-14, and its span is printed in kcal/mol rounded to six decimals (0.000000)
with the Ha figure in brackets. Note which of the two is which - the bracketed value is
Ha, not kcal/mol.

